On 11/08/2012 04:49 PM, Marcos Sanches wrote:
> I am trying to fit a moderated mediation model where my moderator is a 3
> levels categorical variable. This is my syntax:
>
> model2 <- '#Regressions
>
> Y ~ c*X + b*M
>
> M ~ a*X
>
> #variances and covariances
>
> Y ~~ Y
>
> M ~~ M
>
> #indirect effect
>
> ab := a*b
>
> #total effect
>
> tot := c + (a*b)'
>
>
> fit3 <- sem(model2, data = semdata, group = "Treatment", test = "bootstrap")
> summary(fit3)
>
> This does not give me the defined parameter (indirect effect) ab by
> group. I would like to access it by group so that I can compare and see
> if the indirect effect depends on group. Is there a way to get the
> indirect effect for each group?

You have separate regression coefficient per group. So there is no
single 'a' or 'b' or 'c', but you have 'a1,a2,a3', 'b1,b2,b3' and
'c1,c2,c3'.

You can adapt your syntax as follows:

Y ~ c(c1,c2,c3)*X + c(b1,b2,b3)*M
M ~ c(a1,a2,a3)*X
...
ab1 := a1*b1
ab2 := a2*b2
ab3 := a3*b3

tot1 := c1 + (a1*b1)
tot2 := c2 + (a2*b2)
tot3 := c3 + (a3*b3)

Hope this helps,

Yves.

