The multiple group feature for categorical variables is fully
implemented. However:

> library(lavaan)
> n <-300
> x <-rnorm(n)
> y <-rnorm(n)
> z1 <-sample(0:1,n,replace=TRUE)# binary outcome as integer
> z2 <-factor(z1,ordered=TRUE)# binary outcome as factor

> g <-factor(sample(0:1,n,replace=TRUE),labels=c("A","B"))# grouping variable
> df <-data.frame(x,y,z1,z2,g)
>

> # ... but not with a categorical DV:
> s2 <-sem("z2 ~ x+y",data=df,ordered="z2",group="g")
> summary(s2)

Confirmed. This *is* a bug in 0.5-10. And has been added to the 'bugs'
list on the website. However, it only affects models with a _single_
categorical endogenous variable (eg probit regression models).

Larger models (with more than one categorical variable) seem to run fine.

Yves.

