> successful as expected.. anyway
>
> please find the revision below. furthermore i copy-pasted the results
> from the same code having been executed with lavaan versions 0.5.10. and
> 0.4.14:

Confirmed. This is a result of a bug in 0.5-10 (which was reported in
the context of (composite latent variables), where zero-variances are
set to 1, affecting all post-fitting operations, including predict().

To be clear, this bug will only manifest itself if a variance (here, the
residual variance for y) needs to be set to zero. It does not affect
estimation, nor the summary results.

The good news is: this bug was already fixed in the dev version. To
install the dev version, type this in R:

install.packages("pbivnorm")
install.packages("lavaan", repos="http:/www.da.ugent.be <http://www.da.ugent.be>", type="source")

Yves.

